    "content": "The Oscars are held at the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, California, which has served as the permanent home of the Academy Awards ceremony since 2001. Located at Ovation Hollywood on Hollywood Boulevard, the 3,400-seat theater is known for its advanced Dolby Atmos sound and Dolby Vision projection technology. Dolby Theatre Location: 6801 Hollywood Blvd, Hollywood, CA 90028. History: Formerly known as the Kodak Theater, it was explicitly built to host the ceremony, according to the Dolby Theatre website. Design: The stage is frequently redesigned to keep the ceremony fresh while maintaining traditional elegance, with designers working on the set months in advance, says the Los Angeles Times. Surroundings: The theater is located in a complex containing retail shops, restaurants, and is directly connected to the historic TCL Chinese Theatre, notes the Facebook post from Entertainment Weekly. Contract: The Dolby Theatre is scheduled to host the Academy Awards through 2028. Other Academy-managed spaces exist, including the David Geffen Theater and Ted Mann Theater, but the Dolby is the primary venue for the televised show, according to the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences. Other Academy-managed spaces exist, including the David Geffen Theater and Ted Mann Theater, but the Dolby is the primary venue for the televised show, according to the",
